cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "YuhoLens-14B: A Japanese-Finance Fine-Tune for Span-Grounded Investor Memo Generation"
message: "If you use this software or the released model, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Javier
    family-names: De Jesus
    email: javier.dejesusj9@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent
repository-code: "https://github.com/javierdejesusda/YuhoLens"
url: "https://huggingface.co/yuholens/yuholens-14b"
abstract: >-
  YuhoLens-14B is a 14-billion-parameter Japanese-to-English investor-memo
  generation model, produced by full-parameter supervised fine-tuning of
  pfnet/nekomata-14b-pfn-qfin on Japanese 有価証券報告書 (Yuho) filings drawn
  from the SakanaAI/EDINET-Bench corpus. The shipping artefact is a
  4-node LangGraph pipeline whose MemoCriticAgent picks the best
  candidate from N decoder profiles per prompt, achieving KG-2 PASS at
  coherence 3.88 (gate 3.80), citation rate 1.000, and section coverage
  0.994. Built for the AMD Developer Hackathon (lablab.ai, May 2026).
keywords:
  - large-language-model
  - japanese-finance
  - yuho
  - edinet
  - rocm
